		<div class=3D"entry-content">
		<p>The DL-3422 is an LED display similar to the <a href=3D"https://arnowe=
lzel.de/en/led-display-dl-2416-hdlo-2416">DL-2416</a> and the <a href=3D"ht=
tps://arnowelzel.de/en/led-display-dl-3416">DL-3416</a> and was released in=
 the early 1980s. Due to lack of demand, it was only produced for a few yea=
rs and is therefore a fairly rare model. It still appears in a <a href=3D"h=
ttps://archive.org/details/bitsavers_siemens198nicsCatalog_24729432/page/78=
/mode/2up" class=3D"urlexternal">Siemens catalog from 1985</a>, but it alre=
ady has the note =E2=80=9Cphasing out =E2=80=93 not recommended for new des=
ign=E2=80=9D. I don=E2=80=99t know the exact age of my copies, but if I ass=
ume a production date between 1982 and 1985, it=E2=80=99s almost 40 years.<=
/p>
<p><a href=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/11/s=
iemens-dl-3422.jpg" data-lbwps-width=3D"1920" data-lbwps-height=3D"1080" da=
ta-lbwps-srcsmall=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/20=
23/11/siemens-dl-3422-400x225.jpg"><img fetchpriority=3D"high" decoding=3D"=
async" class=3D"alignnone size-large wp-image-6122" src=3D"https://arnowelz=
el.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/11/siemens-dl-3422-800x450.jpg" al=
t=3D"Siemens DL-3422" width=3D"800" height=3D"450"></a></p>
<p><span id=3D"more-6117"></span></p>
<p>A special feature compared to the DL-2416 is the use of 22 segments, whi=
ch also allow descenders for lowercase letters. This makes it possible to d=
isplay the complete ASCII character set. The following view shows an enlarg=
ed view of a display chip and next to it the graphic layout.</p>
<p><a href=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/11/d=
l3422-detail.jpg" data-lbwps-width=3D"575" data-lbwps-height=3D"837" data-l=
bwps-srcsmall=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/1=
1/dl3422-detail-275x400.jpg"><img decoding=3D"async" class=3D"image40 align=
none wp-image-6120 size-large" src=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/wp-content/u=
ploads/sites/2/2023/11/dl3422-detail-550x800.jpg" alt=3D"DL-3422, detail vi=
ew" width=3D"550" height=3D"800"></a> <a class=3D"ml-2" href=3D"https://arn=
owelzel.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/11/dl3422-layout.svg" data-lb=
wps-width=3D"334" data-lbwps-height=3D"554" data-lbwps-srcsmall=3D"https://=
arnowelzel.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/11/dl3422-layout.svg"><img=
 decoding=3D"async" class=3D"image40 alignnone wp-image-6121 size-full" rol=
e=3D"img" src=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/1=
1/dl3422-layout.svg" alt=3D"DL-3422, layout" width=3D"167" height=3D"277"><=
/a></p>
<p>The following information is based on the information from the Siemens c=
atalog from 1985.</p>
<h2>Technical data</h2>
<p>The operating voltage is +5 volts and the module works at TTL levels. In=
put voltages below 0.8 volts are interpreted as =E2=80=9Clow=E2=80=9D or =
=E2=80=9C0=E2=80=9D, levels above 2 volts are interpreted as =E2=80=9Chigh=
=E2=80=9D or =E2=80=9C1=E2=80=9D. This means that controlling it with the G=
PIO outputs of a Raspberry Pi or Arduino or Atmel AVR is no problem.</p>
<p>Depending on the number of LEDs lit at the same time, the current requir=
ement is a maximum of 160 mA, which corresponds to 0.8 watts at 5 volts. If=
 you combine four modules into a display with 16 characters, you have to ex=
pect a maximum power requirement of around 3.2 watts.</p>
<h2>Case and pinout</h2>
<p>Similar to the <a href=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/led-display-dl-2416-h=
dlo-2416">DL-2416</a>, the pin format corresponds to a wide DIL socket with=
 a 2.54 mm pitch, but there are only 22 pins. Suitable bases for this are u=
sually not available. Therefore, you have to use socket strips for plug-in =
installation.</p>
<p>The position of pin 1 is not visually marked on my copies. I therefore h=
ad to make do with examining the displays under a magnifying glass to ensur=
e that they were aligned correctly.</p>
<p><a href=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/11/d=
l3422.png" data-lbwps-width=3D"756" data-lbwps-height=3D"470" data-lbwps-sr=
csmall=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2023/11/dl342=
2-400x249.png"><img loading=3D"lazy" decoding=3D"async" class=3D"image40 al=
ignleft wp-image-6118 size-large" src=3D"https://arnowelzel.de/en/wp-conten=
t/uploads/sites/2/2023/11/dl3422.png" alt=3D"DL-3422" width=3D"756" height=
=3D"470"></a></p>
<table class=3D"framed">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Pin</th>
<th>Function</th>
<th>Pin</th>
<th>Function</th>
</tr>
<tr>
